  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Outriders",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/4835/450x258/outriders-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786935600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/4835-buy-outriders-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Beerfreak",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "Avoid this broken mess\n\n\n\nEven with everything gutted to Low, the game still collapses below 30 FPS during combat on my GTX 1060. For a fast-paced shooter, that’s completely unacceptable.\n\n\n\nAnd then there’s the forced always-online requirement for a supposedly single-player campaign. Your internet connection is part of the fucking game whether you want it or not. A connection hiccup can kick you out of the experience, because apparently a solo campaign wasn’t allowed to simply work offline.\n\n\n\nThe combat is merely decent, the story is painfully generic, and the technical state makes even that mediocre experience miserable.\n\n\n\nDon’t waste your money on this garbage. Not even for €10. Not even for €5. If you want a functional single-player sci-fi shooter, look elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "game": "Splasher",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/1939/450x258/splasher-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786935600",
